.SH "NAME"
nvme-feat-int-vector-config \- Get and set interrupt vector configuration feature
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fIfeat int\-vector\-config\fR <device>
                        [\-\-iv=<iv> | \-i <iv>] [\-\-cd | \-c]
                        [\-\-sel=<select> | \-S <select>] [\-\-save | \-s]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Get and set interrupt vector configuration feature\&.
.sp
The <device> parameter is mandatory and may be either the NVMe character device (ex: /dev/nvme0), or a namespace block device (ex: /dev/nvme0n1)\&.
.sp
If any of the setting options (\-\-iv or \-\-cd) are specified, the command will update the interrupt vector configuration\&. If none of these options are specified, it will retrieve and display the current configuration\&.
.sp
On success it returns 0, error code otherwise\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-i <iv>, \-\-iv=<iv>
.RS 4
Interrupt Vector\&. Specifies the interrupt vector to use for this configuration\&. The value is the number of the interrupt vector\&.
.RE
.PP
\-c, \-\-cd
.RS 4
Coalescing Disable\&. When set, this flag disables interrupt coalescing for the specified interrupt vector\&.
.RE
.PP
\-S <select>, \-\-sel=<select>
.RS 4
Select (SEL): This field specifies which value of the attributes to return in the provided data:
.RE
.PP
\-s, \-\-save
.RS 4
Save the attribute so that it persists through all power states and resets\&.
.RE
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following options are defined at the top\-level nvme command and are available to this subcommand:
.PP
\-\-dry\-run
.RS 4
Print the command that would be executed, but do not actually execute it\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-ioctl\-probing
.RS 4
Disable probing for 64\-bit IOCTL support\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-retries
.RS 4
Disable retry logic on transient errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\-o <fmt>, \-\-output\-format=<fmt>
.RS 4
Set the reporting format to
\fInormal\fR,
\fItabular, \*(Aqjson\fR, or
\fIbinary\fR\&. Only one output format may be used at a time\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-output\-format\-version=<version>
.RS 4
Select the output format version\&. Version
\fI1\fR
uses the original field naming, while version
\fI2\fR
(default) provides more consistent and script\-friendly field names\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-timeout=<ms>
.RS 4
Set the timeout for the command in milliseconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\-v, \-\-verbose
.RS 4
Increase the level of detail in the output\&. May be specified multiple times to further increase verbosity\&.
.RE
.sp
These options can also be set as machine\-wide defaults in nvme\-cli\&.conf(5)\&. A command\-line flag always overrides the file\&.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Has the program issue a feat int\-vector\-config to get the current configuration:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
# nvme feat int\-vector\-config /dev/nvme0
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Has the program issue a feat int\-vector\-config to set the interrupt vector and disable coalescing:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
# nvme feat int\-vector\-config /dev/nvme0 \-\-iv=0 \-\-cd \-\-save
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.RE
